The two main reasons for using disaggregated prefilling in vLLM are:

- Tuning time-to-first-token (TTFT) and inter-token-latency (ITL) separately.
- Controlling tail ITL.
Time: 21,4s
Expected: The two main reasons for using disaggregated prefilling in vLLM are: 1) tuning time-to-first-token (TTFT) and inter-token-latency (ITL) separately by putting prefill and decode phases in different vLLM instances with different parallel strategies, and 2) controlling tail ITL by preventing prefill jobs from being inserted during decoding, which reduces tail latency more reliably than chunked prefill approaches.

